#
# Every minute: the connections open to or from an address the blocked devices' alias has just
# gained are cut (cut.py) - a block rule stops new connections only, and the alias gains an address
# when a listed device takes a new one. Apply cuts what the devices listed have open already. With no
# device listed, or Port Guard off, it reads config.xml once and exits.

* * * * * root /usr/local/opnsense/scripts/portguard/cut.py > /dev/null 2>&1
#
# Every minute: automatic isolation (isolate.py) - a device os-netreport saw reaching a
# command-and-control list in the last 10 minutes isolated by its MAC address, an isolation that ran
# out let go, the isolated devices' table kept. With the option off and nothing isolated, it reads
# config.xml, asks pf whether that table still holds an address (pfctl -T show), and exits.
* * * * * root /usr/local/opnsense/scripts/portguard/isolate.py run > /dev/null 2>&1
